input.content:
# Tasks

This change depends on `mcp-session-access` (Roam page `Spec: MCP token handoff`). It needs four things from it:

- the handoff;
- the `mcp_session` registry;
- the plugin connect command;
- the two password settings, which this change needs in v0.

Groups 1, 4, 5 and 7 need it landed.

Each `## N.` group is one proposed Linear ticket. Its `Carries:` line names the requirements and decisions it implements, and those scenarios are the ticket's Done When.

## 1. Read-only session role (`packages/database`)

Carries: `agent-read-access` "The database refuses writes from handed-over sessions" and "Handed-over sessions cannot change the space password"; design Decision 4.

- [ ] 1.1 Add the `mcp_reader` role. Grant it to `authenticator`, and give it `SELECT` on the tables and views retrieval reads. Verify: `pnpm check-schema` passes, and a cucumber scenario shows that `mcp_reader` reads only what the space account can read.
- [ ] 1.2 Revoke `EXECUTE` on `public` functions from `PUBLIC`, including the default privileges. Grant `mcp_reader` `EXECUTE` on an allowlist of the access helpers that policies and views call. Verify:
  - a test lists every function `mcp_reader` can execute, and matches it against the allowlist;
  - the full cucumber suite still passes as `anon` and `authenticated`.
- [ ] 1.3 Add a custom access token hook. When the token's `session_id` is in `mcp_session`, it sets `role` to `mcp_reader`. Otherwise it returns the claims unchanged. Enable it in `config.toml`, and document how to enable it on the hosted project. Verify: cucumber scenarios for
  - an MCP session getting `mcp_reader` on issue and on refresh;
  - a plugin session keeping `authenticated`.
- [ ] 1.4 Verify that writes are refused. Verify: cucumber scenarios showing that a handed-over session fails to
  - insert, update or delete a node;
  - call `create_secret_token`;
  - call `accept_group_invitation`;
  - call an upsert function.

  The same writes succeed with the plugin's session.
- [ ] 1.5 Confirm that `secure_password_change` and "require current password" are on in the hosted project. Verify: a password change made with a handed-over session is refused, recorded against the hosted project, because "require current password" can't be set in `config.toml`.

## 2. Retrieval functions (`packages/database`)

Carries: `discourse-retrieval` "Readable synced collection", "Nodes and types are identified by rid", "Full node text", "Readable type discovery and filtering" (discovery side) and "One-hop discourse context"; `agent-read-access` "Per-space principal" and "Current permissions"; design Decisions 2, 5 and 7.

- [ ] 2.1 Add get-node, built on `getSharedNodeByRid`.
  - Fetch the `full` Content as import does, and add `typeRid`.
  - Map `null` to `not_found`.
  - Map a conversion failure or a missing `full` Content to `content_unavailable`.

  Verify: cucumber scenarios on Roam and Obsidian fixtures for
  - a readable node;
  - an unreadable node returning the same `not_found` as a missing one;
  - a missing `full` Content;
  - a stored empty body.

  The returned `rid` matches discovery's.
- [ ] 2.2 Add type discovery: the types present on readable node instances, identified by type `rid` and labelled with `dbNodeSchemasToCrossApp`. Verify: cucumber scenarios for
  - types that appear only on readable nodes;
  - two same-named types in different spaces.
- [ ] 2.3 Add one-hop context.
  - Read the readable relation instances whose `refs` contain the node.
  - Take direction from `reference_content`.
  - Convert them with `dbRelationsToCrossApp`.

  Verify: cucumber scenarios for
  - incoming and outgoing relations;
  - an excluded unreadable endpoint;
  - a self-link in both directions;
  - excluded ordinary backlinks.
- [ ] 2.4 Run 2.1-2.3 as `mcp_reader`. Verify: cucumber scenarios showing that
  - a private node in another space isn't returned;
  - a node shared from another space is returned;
  - access gained or lost after handoff applies without a new session.

## 3. Search (`packages/database`)

Carries: `discourse-retrieval` "Existing semantic search", "Bounded search without a relevance cutoff" and "Readable type discovery and filtering" (filter side); design Decision 6.

- [ ] 3.1 Add a `SECURITY INVOKER` search RPC. It takes a 1536-dimension vector, optional type `rid`s and a limit. It:
  - joins the current non-obsolete `direct` and `direct_and_description` embeddings of readable node instances;
  - keeps each node's best similarity once;
  - filters and deduplicates before the limit;
  - sorts by similarity, then by `rid`;
  - applies no threshold.

  Leave `match_content_embeddings` unchanged. Verify: cucumber scenarios with deterministic vectors for
  - type filtering before the limit;
  - one result per node;
  - a returned negative similarity;
  - an absent node without an embedding;
  - `match_content_embeddings` results unchanged.
- [ ] 3.2 Add the search function. It calls the RPC and converts the hits with `dbNodesToCrossApp`. It adds `score`, `typeRid`, and an excerpt of the first 300 code points of the body, falling back to `content.direct`. Verify: tests for both excerpt sources, and for a multi-byte character at the cut.
- [ ] 3.3 Grant `EXECUTE` on the RPC to `mcp_reader`, and regenerate `dbTypes`. Verify: `pnpm lint`, `pnpm check-types` and `pnpm check-schema` pass.

## 4. Retrieval API (`apps/website`)

Carries: `headless-retrieval-api` "Four retrieval operations", "Handed-over sessions only", "Versioned contract" and "Headless retrieval after setup"; design Decisions 1, 6 and 8.

