  - Fetch the `full` Content as import does, and add `typeRid`.
  - Map `null` to `not_found`.
  - Map a conversion failure or a missing `full` Content to `content_unavailable`.

  Verify: cucumber scenarios on Roam and Obsidian fixtures for
  - a readable node;
  - an unreadable node returning the same `not_found` as a missing one;
  - a missing `full` Content;
  - a stored empty body.

  The returned `rid` matches discovery's.
- [ ] 2.2 Add type discovery: the types present on readable node instances, identified by type `rid` and labelled with `dbNodeSchemasToCrossApp`. Verify: cucumber scenarios for
  - types that appear only on readable nodes;
  - two same-named types in different spaces.
- [ ] 2.3 Add one-hop context.
  - Read the readable relation instances whose `refs` contain the node.
  - Take direction from `reference_content`.
  - Convert them with `dbRelationsToCrossApp`.

  Verify: cucumber scenarios for
  - incoming and outgoing relations;
  - an excluded unreadable endpoint;
  - a self-link in both directions;
  - excluded ordinary backlinks.
- [ ] 2.4 Run 2.1-2.3 as `mcp_reader`. Verify: cucumber scenarios showing that
  - a private node in another space isn't returned;
  - a node shared from another space is returned;
  - access gained or lost after handoff applies without a new session.

## 3. Search (`packages/database`)

Carries: `discourse-retrieval` "Existing semantic search", "Bounded search without a relevance cutoff" and "Readable type discovery and filtering" (filter side); design Decision 6.

- [ ] 3.1 Add a `SECURITY INVOKER` search RPC. It takes a 1536-dimension vector, optional type `rid`s and a limit. It:
  - joins the current non-obsolete `direct` and `direct_and_description` embeddings of readable node instances;
  - keeps each node's best similarity once;
  - filters and deduplicates before the limit;
  - sorts by similarity, then by `rid`;
  - applies no threshold.

  Leave `match_content_embeddings` unchanged. Verify: cucumber scenarios with deterministic vectors for
  - type filtering before the limit;
  - one result per node;
  - a returned negative similarity;
  - an absent node without an embedding;
  - `match_content_embeddings` results unchanged.
- [ ] 3.2 Add the search function. It calls the RPC and converts the hits with `dbNodesToCrossApp`. It adds `score`, `typeRid`, and an excerpt of the first 300 code points of the body, falling back to `content.direct`. Verify: tests for both excerpt sources, and for a multi-byte character at the cut.
- [ ] 3.3 Grant `EXECUTE` on the RPC to `mcp_reader`, and regenerate `dbTypes`. Verify: `pnpm lint`, `pnpm check-types` and `pnpm check-schema` pass.

## 4. Retrieval API (`apps/website`)

Carries: `headless-retrieval-api` "Four retrieval operations", "Handed-over sessions only", "Versioned contract" and "Headless retrieval after setup"; design Decisions 1, 6 and 8.

- [ ] 4.1 Add the Zod input schemas and error codes from Decision 8. Verify: `pnpm test:unit` covers
  - a blank query;
  - a malformed `rid`;
  - an empty explicit type list;
  - the limit default of 10, and rejection outside 1-30.
- [ ] 4.2 Add a request-scoped auth helper. It validates the bearer token with Supabase Auth, rejects any `role` other than `mcp_reader` with `forbidden`, and builds a client that acts as the caller. Verify: integration tests that
  - a missing, invalid or expired token returns 401;
  - a plugin session token returns 403;
  - a handed-over session token returns data.
- [ ] 4.3 Add the four `/api/v1` routes over the group 2 and 3 functions, with the HTTP codes from Decision 8. Search embeds the query on the server through the shared OpenAI helper, after authentication. Verify: `pnpm test:integration` in `apps/website` covers each route's success and error cases, and an embedding failure returning 503.
- [ ] 4.4 Enforce complete-or-error responses against a 1 MiB budget, and keep logs to the fields in Decision 8. Verify:
  - an integration test for `result_too_large`;
  - a log capture that contains no `Authorization` header, query text or body.

## 5. Local MCP (`apps/mcp`, location proposed)

Carries: `discourse-mcp` "Tools are thin clients of the API" and "Distribution and setup"; design Decision 9.

- [ ] 5.1 Scaffold a stdio server on the MCP TypeScript SDK that logs only to stderr. Verify: a test asserts that nothing but protocol messages reaches stdout.
- [ ] 5.2 Add `connect --name <name>`. It reads the bundle from stdin, refreshes once, checks that the `role` claim is `mcp_reader`, and writes `~/.discourse-graphs/mcp/<name>.json` with mode 0600. Verify: unit tests for success, a wrong role, and the file mode.
- [ ] 5.3 On start, the MCP loads the state file, takes a lock, and refuses to run without `mcp_reader`. It writes each rotated refresh token atomically before using it. Verify: unit tests that
  - a refresh writes the new token;
  - a second process exits with a clear error;
  - a wrong role stops startup.
- [ ] 5.4 Implement the four tools. Each calls one `/api/v1` route with the current access token, returns structured content plus a compact text form, and passes API error codes through as tool errors. An unreachable API is `dependency_error`. Every tool carries a read-only annotation. Verify: per-tool unit tests against a mocked API for
  - success;
  - each error code;
  - an unreachable API.

  Another test checks that the listed tools are exactly these four.
- [ ] 5.5 Add `token --name <name>`. It prints a current access token from the connection's state file, refreshing under the lock. Verify: a unit test that it refreshes an expired token and writes the rotated refresh token.

## 6. Distribution and docs

Carries: `discourse-mcp` "Distribution and setup" and "Supported agent clients"; `headless-retrieval-api` "Documented developer contract"; design Decision 9.

- [ ] 6.1 Publish `@discourse-graphs/mcp` (name proposed) to npm from CI, with semver releases. Verify: a dry-run publish runs in CI, and one published prerelease installs and runs with `npx`.
- [ ] 6.2 Write the MCP setup README for Claude Code, Claude Desktop and Codex. It covers
  - connect;
  - one bundle and `--name` per client;
  - the state file risk;
  - search limits;
  - sync-gap errors;
  - that ChatGPT is unsupported.

  Verify: someone outside the change follows it in each client.
- [ ] 6.3 Write the API docs. They cover
  - getting a token with `token --name`;
  - a `curl` example for each route;
  - errors;
  - search limits;
  - the per-space model;
  - that unimported readable nodes can appear;
  - weak matches;
  - no pagination.

  Verify: each example runs against a test space.

## 7. End-to-end validation and release

Carries: `discourse-mcp` "Supported agent clients"; `headless-retrieval-api` "Headless retrieval after setup"; `agent-read-access` "Session sign-out" and "The database refuses writes from handed-over sessions".

- [ ] 7.1 Install the MCP in Claude Desktop, Claude Code and Codex with a test space's bundle. Complete all four operations with Roam and Obsidian closed. Verify: client versions and one transcript per client are recorded in the PR.
- [ ] 7.2 In each client, ask the agent to change a node through a direct Supabase call, using the state file's session. Verify: the database refuses it, recorded in the PR.
- [ ] 7.3 Sign out the session with local scope. Verify: it can't refresh, and MCP and API requests fail once its access token expires.
- [ ] 7.4 Release to a limited validation cohort. Verify: cohort members complete setup and run all four operations before a wider release.

## Follow-ups outside this change

- Archive with `/opsx:archive` once every group has landed.
- Decide whether one agent should span several spaces.

