content.content:
- # Tasks
  - This change depends on `mcp-session-access` ([[Spec: MCP token handoff]]). It needs three things from it:
    - the handoff;
    - the `mcp_session` registry;
    - the plugin connect command.
  - Groups 1, 4, 5 and 7 need it landed.
  - Each `## N.` group is one proposed Linear ticket. Its `Carries:` line names the requirements and decisions it implements, and those scenarios are the ticket's Done When.
  - ## 1. Read-only session role (`packages/database`)
    - Carries: `agent-read-access` "The database refuses writes from handed-over sessions" and "Handed-over sessions cannot replace the space login"; design Decision 4.
    - {{[[TODO]]}} 1.1 Add the `mcp_reader` role. Grant it to `authenticator`, and give it `SELECT` on the tables and views retrieval reads. Verify: `pnpm check-schema` passes, and a cucumber scenario shows that `mcp_reader` reads only what the space account can read.
    - {{[[TODO]]}} 1.2 Revoke `EXECUTE` on `public` functions from `PUBLIC`, including the default privileges. Grant `mcp_reader` `EXECUTE` on an allowlist of the access helpers that policies and views call. Verify:
      - a test lists every function `mcp_reader` can execute, and matches it against the allowlist;
      - the full cucumber suite still passes as `anon` and `authenticated`.
    - {{[[TODO]]}} 1.3 Add a custom access token hook. When the token's `session_id` is in `mcp_session`, it sets `role` to `mcp_reader`. Otherwise it returns the claims unchanged. Enable it in `config.toml`, and document how to enable it on the hosted project. Verify: cucumber scenarios for
      - an MCP session getting `mcp_reader` on issue and on refresh;
      - a plugin session keeping `authenticated`.
    - {{[[TODO]]}} 1.4 Verify that writes are refused. Verify: cucumber scenarios showing that a handed-over session fails to
      - insert, update or delete a node;
      - call `create_secret_token`;
      - call `accept_group_invitation`;
      - call an upsert function.
      - The same writes succeed with the plugin's session.
    - {{[[TODO]]}} 1.5 Turn on the space login lock. Set `secure_password_change` in `config.toml` and on the hosted project. Set "require current password" on the hosted project only, because `config.toml` has no key for it. Verify: an attempt to replace the space login with a session token is refused, recorded against the hosted project.
  - ## 2. Retrieval functions (`packages/database`)
    - Carries: `discourse-retrieval` "Readable synced collection", "Nodes and types are identified by rid", "Full node text", "Readable type discovery and filtering" (discovery side) and "One-hop discourse context"; `agent-read-access` "Per-space principal" and "Current permissions"; design Decisions 2, 5 and 7.
    - {{[[TODO]]}} 2.1 Add get-node, built on `getSharedNodeByRid`.
      - Fetch the `full` Content as import does, and add `typeRid`.
      - Map `null` to `not_found`.
      - Map a conversion failure or a missing `full` Content to `content_unavailable`.
      - Verify: cucumber scenarios on Roam and Obsidian fixtures for
        - a readable node;
        - an unreadable node returning the same `not_found` as a missing one;
        - a missing `full` Content;
        - a stored empty body.
        - The returned `rid` matches discovery's.
    - {{[[TODO]]}} 2.2 Add type discovery: the types present on readable node instances, identified by type `rid` and labelled with `dbNodeSchemasToCrossApp`. Verify: cucumber scenarios for
      - types that appear only on readable nodes;
      - two same-named types in different spaces.
    - {{[[TODO]]}} 2.3 Add one-hop context.
      - Read the readable relation instances whose `refs` contain the node.
      - Take direction from `reference_content`.
      - Convert them with `dbRelationsToCrossApp`.
      - Verify: cucumber scenarios for
        - incoming and outgoing relations;
        - an excluded unreadable endpoint;
        - a self-link in both directions;
        - excluded ordinary backlinks.
    - {{[[TODO]]}} 2.4 Run 2.1-2.3 as `mcp_reader`. Verify: cucumber scenarios showing that
      - a private node in another space isn't returned;
      - a node shared from another space is returned;
      - access gained or lost after handoff applies without a new session.
  - ## 3. Search (`packages/database`)
    - Carries: `discourse-retrieval` "Existing semantic search", "Bounded search without a relevance cutoff" and "Readable type discovery and filtering" (filter side); design Decision 6.
    - {{[[TODO]]}} 3.1 Add a `SECURITY INVOKER` search RPC. It takes a 1536-dimension vector, optional type `rid`s and a limit. It:
      - joins the current non-obsolete `direct` and `direct_and_description` embeddings of readable node instances;
      - keeps each node's best similarity once;
      - filters and deduplicates before the limit;
      - sorts by similarity, then by `rid`;
      - applies no threshold.

