- [ ] 2.4 Run 2.1-2.3 as `mcp_reader` (read-only database role). Verify: cucumber scenarios showing that
  - a private node in another space isn't returned;
  - a node shared from another space is returned;
  - access gained or lost after handoff applies without a new session.

## 3. Hybrid search (`packages/database`)

Carries: `discourse-retrieval` "Hybrid search over titles and descriptions", "Bounded search without a relevance cutoff" and "Readable type discovery and filtering" (filter side); design Decision 6.

- [ ] 3.1 Add a generated full-text column (`tsvector`, a keyword index) on `Content` (the text table) for the `direct` (title) and `direct_and_description` (title plus description) variants. Use the `simple` text configuration, and add a GIN index. Verify: `pnpm check-schema` passes, and a sync of a test space still succeeds.
- [ ] 3.2 Add a `SECURITY INVOKER` (runs as the caller) search RPC, adapted from [Supabase's hybrid search recipe](https://supabase.com/docs/guides/ai/hybrid-search). It takes query text, a 1536-dimension vector, optional type `rid`s and a limit. It:
  - builds a keyword list (`websearch_to_tsquery`, ranked by `ts_rank_cd`) and a semantic list (cosine similarity over current non-obsolete embeddings), both over readable node instances;
  - type-filters each list, and keeps each node once, before taking up to twice the limit as candidates;
  - merges the lists with Reciprocal Rank Fusion (weights 1, `rrf_k` 50);
  - sorts by fused score, then by `rid`;
  - applies the limit, with no threshold.

  Leave `match_content_embeddings` (the existing semantic search query) unchanged. Verify: cucumber scenarios with deterministic vectors for
  - a keyword-only match that is returned;
  - a semantic-only match that is returned;
  - type filtering before the limit;
  - one result per node;
  - a weak match returned when it is under the limit;
  - unchanged results from `match_content_embeddings`.
- [ ] 3.3 Add the search function. It calls the RPC, converts hits with `dbNodesToCrossApp` (converts nodes), and adds `score`, `typeRid` and an excerpt. The excerpt is the first 300 code points of the body, falling back to the title. Verify: tests for both excerpt sources, and for a multi-byte character at the cut.
