- [ ] 5.2 Add `connect --name <name>`. It reads the bundle from stdin, refreshes once, and checks that the `role` claim is `mcp_reader` (read-only database role). It then writes `~/.discourse-graphs/mcp/<name>.json` with mode 0600. Verify: unit tests for success, a wrong role, and the file mode.
- [ ] 5.3 On start, the MCP loads the state file, takes a lock, and refuses to run without `mcp_reader`. It writes each rotated refresh token atomically before using it. Verify: unit tests that
  - a refresh writes the new token;
  - a second process exits with a clear error;
  - a wrong role stops startup.
- [ ] 5.4 Implement the four tools.
  - Each calls one `/api/v1` route with the current session token.
  - Each returns structured content plus a compact text form.
  - Each passes API error codes through as tool errors. An unreachable API is `dependency_error`.
  - Every tool carries a read-only annotation, and its input definition is generated from the shared Zod schema.

  Verify: per-tool unit tests against a mocked API for
  - success;
  - each error code;
  - an unreachable API.

  Another test checks that the listed tools are exactly these four.
- [ ] 5.5 Add `token --name <name>`. It prints a current session token from the connection's state file, refreshing under the lock. Verify: a unit test that it refreshes an expired session token and writes the rotated refresh token.

## 6. Distribution and docs

Carries: `discourse-mcp` "Distribution and setup" and "Supported agent clients"; `headless-retrieval-api` "Documented developer contract"; design Decision 9.

- [ ] 6.1 Publish `@discourse-graphs/mcp` (name proposed) to npm from CI, with semver releases. Verify: a dry-run publish runs in CI, and one published prerelease installs and runs with `npx`.
- [ ] 6.2 Write the MCP setup README for Claude Code, Claude Desktop and Codex. It covers
  - connect;
  - one bundle and one `--name` per client;
  - the state file risk;
  - search limits;
  - sync-gap errors;
  - that ChatGPT is unsupported.

  Verify: someone outside the change follows it in each client.
- [ ] 6.3 Write the API docs. They cover
  - getting a session token with `token --name`;
  - a `curl` example for each route;
  - errors;
  - search limits;
  - the per-space model;
  - that readable nodes can appear even if they were never imported;
  - weak matches;
  - that there's no pagination.

  Verify: each example runs against a test space, and a check compares the documented inputs, outputs and error codes with the shared Zod schemas.

## 7. End-to-end validation and release

Carries: `discourse-mcp` "Supported agent clients"; `headless-retrieval-api` "Headless retrieval after setup"; `agent-read-access` "Session sign-out" and "The database refuses writes from handed-over sessions".

- [ ] 7.1 Install the MCP in Claude Desktop, Claude Code and Codex with a test space's bundle. Complete all four operations with Roam and Obsidian closed. Verify: client versions, and one transcript per client, are recorded in the PR.
- [ ] 7.2 In each client, ask the agent to change a node through a direct Supabase call, using the state file's session. Verify: the database refuses it, and the refusal is recorded in the PR.
- [ ] 7.3 Sign out the session with local scope, meaning only its own session. Verify: it can't refresh, and MCP and API requests fail once its session token expires.
- [ ] 7.4 Release to a limited validation cohort. Verify: cohort members complete setup and run all four operations before a wider release.

## Follow-ups outside this change

- Archive with `/opsx:archive` once every group has landed.
- Decide whether one agent should span several spaces.

