1	- # Tasks
2	  - This change depends on `mcp-session-access`, the [session handoff spec]([[Spec: MCP token handoff]]). It needs three things from it:
3	    - the handoff;
4	    - the `mcp_session` registry (list of handed-over sessions);
5	    - the plugin connect command.
6	  - Groups 1, 4, 5 and 7 need it landed.
7	  - Each `## N.` group is one proposed Linear ticket. Its `Carries:` line names the requirements and decisions the group implements. Those requirements' scenarios are the ticket's Done When.
8	  - ## 1. Read-only session role (`packages/database`)
9	    - Carries: `agent-read-access` "The database refuses writes from handed-over sessions" and "Handed-over sessions cannot replace the space login"; design Decision 4.
10	    - {{[[TODO]]}} 1.1 Add `mcp_reader` (read-only database role). Grant it to `authenticator` (the role Supabase's REST layer logs in as). Give it `SELECT` on the tables and views retrieval reads. Verify: `pnpm check-schema` passes, and a cucumber scenario shows that `mcp_reader` reads only what the space account can read.
11	    - {{[[TODO]]}} 1.2 Revoke `EXECUTE` on `public` functions from `PUBLIC` (every database role), including the default privileges. Then grant `mcp_reader` `EXECUTE` on an allowlist of the access helpers that policies and views call. Verify:
12	      - a test lists every function `mcp_reader` can execute, and matches it against the allowlist;
13	      - the full cucumber suite still passes as `anon` and as `authenticated`.
14	    - {{[[TODO]]}} 1.3 Add a custom access token hook (assigns a role at sign-in). When the token's `session_id` is in `mcp_session` (list of handed-over sessions), it sets `role` to `mcp_reader`. Otherwise it returns the claims unchanged. Enable it in `config.toml`, and document how to enable it on the hosted project. Verify: cucumber scenarios for
15	      - an MCP session getting `mcp_reader`, both on issue and on refresh;
16	      - a plugin session keeping `authenticated`.
17	    - {{[[TODO]]}} 1.4 Verify that writes are refused. Verify: cucumber scenarios showing that a handed-over session fails to
18	      - insert, update or delete a node;
19	      - call `create_secret_token`;
20	      - call `accept_group_invitation`;
21	      - call an upsert function.
22	      - The same writes succeed with the plugin's session.
23	    - {{[[TODO]]}} 1.5 Turn on the space login lock, which stops a session from replacing the space login.
24	      - Set `secure_password_change` in `config.toml` and on the hosted project.
25	      - Set "require current password" on the hosted project only, because `config.toml` has no key for it.
26	      - Verify: an attempt to replace the space login with a session token is refused. Record the result against the hosted project.
27	  - ## 2. Retrieval functions (`packages/database`)
28	    - Carries: `discourse-retrieval` "Readable synced collection", "Nodes and types are identified by rid", "Full node text", "Readable type discovery and filtering" (discovery side) and "One-hop discourse context"; `agent-read-access` "Per-space principal" and "Current permissions"; design Decisions 2, 5 and 7.
29	    - {{[[TODO]]}} 2.1 Add get-node, built on `getSharedNodeByRid` (reads one node by ID) from [ENG-2091](https://linear.app/discourse-graphs/issue/ENG-2091).
30	      - Fetch the `full` Content (the body) as import does, and add `typeRid`.
31	      - Map `null` to `not_found`.
32	      - Map a conversion failure, or a missing body, to `content_unavailable`.
33	      - Verify: cucumber scenarios on Roam and Obsidian fixtures for
34	        - a readable node;
35	        - an unreadable node, returning the same `not_found` as a missing one;
36	        - a missing body;
37	        - a stored empty body.
38	        - The returned `rid` (global node ID) matches discovery's.
39	    - {{[[TODO]]}} 2.2 Add type discovery: the types present on readable node instances, identified by type `rid` and labelled with `dbNodeSchemasToCrossApp` (converts node types). Verify: cucumber scenarios for
40	      - types that appear only on readable nodes;
