file.content:
# Tasks

This change depends on `mcp-session-access`, the [session handoff spec](https://roamresearch.com/#/app/discourse-graphs/page/kPg_0_-lh). It needs three things from it:

- the handoff;
- the `mcp_session` registry (list of handed-over sessions);
- the plugin connect command.

Groups 1, 4, 5 and 7 need it landed.

Each `## N.` group is one proposed Linear ticket. Its `Carries:` line names the requirements and decisions the group implements. Those requirements' scenarios are the ticket's Done When.

## 1. Read-only session role (`packages/database`)

Carries: `agent-read-access` "The database refuses writes from handed-over sessions" and "Handed-over sessions cannot replace the space login"; design Decision 4.

- [ ] 1.1 Add `mcp_reader` (read-only database role). Grant it to `authenticator` (the role Supabase's REST layer logs in as). Give it `SELECT` on the tables and views retrieval reads. Verify: `pnpm check-schema` passes, and a cucumber scenario shows that `mcp_reader` reads only what the space account can read.
- [ ] 1.2 Revoke `EXECUTE` on `public` functions from `PUBLIC` (every database role), including the default privileges. Then grant `mcp_reader` `EXECUTE` on an allowlist of the access helpers that policies and views call. Verify:
  - a test lists every function `mcp_reader` can execute, and matches it against the allowlist;
  - the full cucumber suite still passes as `anon` and as `authenticated`;
  - before the revoke, a query on the hosted database shows that `anon` and `authenticated` hold `EXECUTE` on every `public` function (`has_function_privilege`).
- [ ] 1.3 Add a custom access token hook (assigns a role at sign-in). When the token's `session_id` is in `mcp_session` (list of handed-over sessions), it sets `role` to `mcp_reader`. Otherwise it returns the claims unchanged. Enable it in `config.toml`, and document how to enable it on the hosted project. Verify: cucumber scenarios for
  - an MCP session getting `mcp_reader`, both on issue and on refresh;
  - a plugin session keeping `authenticated`.
- [ ] 1.4 Verify that writes are refused. Verify: cucumber scenarios showing that a handed-over session fails to
  - insert, update or delete a node;
  - call `create_secret_token`;
  - call `accept_group_invitation`;
  - call an upsert function.

  The same writes succeed with the plugin's session.
- [ ] 1.5 Turn on the space login lock, which stops a session from replacing the space login.
  - Set `secure_password_change` in `config.toml` and on the hosted project.
  - Set "require current password" on the hosted project only, because `config.toml` has no key for it.

  Verify: an attempt to replace the space login with a session token is refused. Record the result against the hosted project.

## 2. Retrieval functions (`packages/database`)

Carries: `discourse-retrieval` "Readable synced collection", "Nodes and types are identified by rid", "Full node text", "Readable type and provenance", "Readable type discovery and filtering" (discovery side) and "One-hop discourse context"; `agent-read-access` "Per-space principal" and "Current permissions"; design Decisions 2, 5 and 7.

- [ ] 2.1 Add get-node, built on `getSharedNodeByRid` (reads one node by ID) from [ENG-2091](https://linear.app/discourse-graphs/issue/ENG-2091).
  - Fetch the `full` Content (the body) as import does.
  - Add `type` (`rid` and name), `author` (name from `my_accounts`), and `sourceUrl` (Roam) or `sourcePath` (Obsidian).
  - Map `null` to `not_found`.
  - Map a conversion failure, or a missing body, to `content_unavailable`.

  Verify: cucumber scenarios on Roam and Obsidian fixtures for
  - a readable node;
  - an unreadable node, returning the same `not_found` as a missing one;
  - a missing body;
  - a stored empty body;
  - the type name, author name and source link or path, on each platform.

  The returned `rid` (global node ID) matches discovery's.
- [ ] 2.2 Add type discovery: the types present on readable node instances, identified by type `rid` and labelled with `dbNodeSchemasToCrossApp` (converts node types). Verify: cucumber scenarios for
  - types that appear only on readable nodes;
  - two same-named types in different spaces.
- [ ] 2.3 Add one-hop context.
  - Read the readable relation instances whose `refs` (list of referenced IDs) contain the node.
  - Take direction from `reference_content` (the relation's endpoint map).
  - Convert them with `dbRelationsToCrossApp` (converts relations).

  Verify: cucumber scenarios for
  - incoming and outgoing relations;
  - an unreadable endpoint, which is excluded;
  - a self-link, in both directions;
  - ordinary backlinks, which are excluded.
- [ ] 2.4 Run 2.1-2.3 as `mcp_reader` (read-only database role). Verify: cucumber scenarios showing that
  - a private node in another space isn't returned;
  - a node shared from another space is returned;
  - access gained or lost after handoff applies without a new session.

## 3. Search (`packages/database`)

Carries: `discourse-retrieval` "Semantic search over existing embeddings", "Search result fields", "Bounded search without a relevance cutoff" and "Readable type discovery and filtering" (filter side); design Decision 6.

- [ ] 3.1 Add a `SECURITY INVOKER` (runs as the caller) search RPC. It takes a 1536-dimension vector, optional type `rid`s and a limit. It:
  - joins the current non-obsolete `direct` (title) and `direct_and_description` (title plus description) embeddings of readable node instances;
  - keeps each node's best similarity once;
  - filters and deduplicates before the limit;
  - sorts by similarity, then by `rid`;
  - applies no threshold.

  Leave `match_content_embeddings` (the existing semantic search query) unchanged. Verify: cucumber scenarios with deterministic vectors for
  - type filtering before the limit;
  - one result per node;
  - a negative similarity that is returned;
  - a node without an embedding, which is absent;
  - unchanged results from `match_content_embeddings`.
- [ ] 3.2 Add the search function. It calls the RPC, converts hits with `dbNodesToCrossApp` (converts nodes), and adds the same `type`, `author` and source fields as get-node, plus `score` and an excerpt. The excerpt is the first 300 code points of the body, falling back to the title. Verify: tests for both excerpt sources, and for a multi-byte character at the cut.
- [ ] 3.3 Grant `EXECUTE` on the RPC to `mcp_reader`, and regenerate `dbTypes`. Verify: `pnpm lint`, `pnpm check-types` and `pnpm check-schema` pass.

## 4. Retrieval API (`apps/website`)

Carries: `headless-retrieval-api` "Four retrieval operations", "Response envelope", "Authenticated sessions", "Versioned contract" and "Headless retrieval after setup"; design Decisions 1, 6 and 8.

- [ ] 4.1 Add the shared Zod input and output schemas (typed request and response definitions) to `packages/database`, along with the response envelope and the error codes from Decision 8. Verify: `pnpm test:unit` covers
  - a blank query;
  - a malformed `rid`;
  - an empty explicit type list;
  - the default limit of 10, and rejection of limits outside 1-30.
- [ ] 4.2 Add a request-scoped auth helper. It validates the session token with Supabase Auth, and builds a client that acts as the caller. Verify: integration tests that
  - a missing, invalid or expired token returns 401;
  - a valid session token returns data.
- [ ] 4.3 Add the four `/api/v1` routes over the group 2 and 3 functions, with the HTTP codes from Decision 8. Search embeds the query on the server after authentication, through an OpenAI helper extracted from `/api/embeddings/openai/small`. That route keeps its behavior. Verify: `pnpm test:integration` in `apps/website` covers each route's success and error cases, the envelope on each, and an embedding failure returning 503.
- [ ] 4.4 Enforce complete-or-error responses against a 1 MiB budget, and keep logs to the fields in Decision 8. Verify:
  - an integration test for `result_too_large`;
  - a log capture that contains no `Authorization` header, query text or body.

## 5. Local MCP (`apps/mcp`, location proposed)

Carries: `discourse-mcp` "Tools are thin clients of the API" and "Distribution and setup"; design Decision 9.

- [ ] 5.1 Scaffold a stdio server on the MCP TypeScript SDK that logs only to stderr. Verify: a test asserts that only protocol messages reach stdout.
- [ ] 5.2 Add `connect --name <name>`. It reads the bundle from stdin, refreshes once, and checks that the `role` claim is `mcp_reader` (read-only database role). It then writes `~/.discourse-graphs/mcp/<name>.json` with mode 0600. Verify: unit tests for success, a wrong role, and the file mode.
- [ ] 5.3 On start, the MCP loads the state file, takes a lock, and refuses to run without `mcp_reader`. It writes each rotated refresh token atomically before using it. Verify: unit tests that
  - a refresh writes the new token;
  - a second process exits with a clear error;
  - a wrong role stops startup.
- [ ] 5.4 Implement the four tools.
  - Each calls one `/api/v1` route with the current session token.
  - Each returns structured content plus a compact text form.
  - Each passes API error codes through as tool errors. An unreachable API is `dependency_error`.
  - Every tool carries a read-only annotation, and its input definition is generated from the shared Zod schema.

  Verify: per-tool unit tests against a mocked API for
  - success;
  - each error code;
  - an unreachable API.

  Another test checks that the listed tools are exactly these four.

## 6. Distribution and docs

Carries: `discourse-mcp` "Distribution and setup" and "Supported agent clients"; design Decision 9.

- [ ] 6.1 Publish `@discourse-graphs/mcp` (name proposed) to npm from CI, with semver releases. Verify: a dry-run publish runs in CI, and one published prerelease installs and runs with `npx`.
- [ ] 6.2 Write the MCP setup README for Claude Code, Claude Desktop and Codex. It covers
  - connect;
  - one bundle and one `--name` per client;
  - the state file risk;
  - search limits, including that search matches titles (and Roam descriptions), not bodies;
  - sync-gap errors;
  - that ChatGPT is unsupported.

  Verify: someone outside the change follows it in each client.

## 7. End-to-end validation and release

Carries: `discourse-mcp` "Supported agent clients"; `headless-retrieval-api` "Headless retrieval after setup"; `agent-read-access` "Session sign-out" and "The database refuses writes from handed-over sessions".

- [ ] 7.1 Install the MCP in Claude Desktop, Claude Code and Codex with a test space's bundle. Complete all four operations with Roam and Obsidian closed. Verify: client versions, and one transcript per client, are recorded in the PR.
- [ ] 7.2 In each client, ask the agent to change a node through a direct Supabase call, using the state file's session. Verify: the database refuses it, and the refusal is recorded in the PR.
- [ ] 7.3 Sign out the session with local scope, meaning only its own session. Verify: it can't refresh, and MCP and API requests fail once its session token expires.
- [ ] 7.4 Release to a limited validation cohort. Verify: cohort members complete setup and run all four operations before a wider release.

## Follow-ups outside this change

- Archive with `/opsx:archive` once every group has landed.
- Decide whether one agent should span several spaces.
- Hybrid search, adapting Supabase's recipe (design Decision 6).

